1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,930
Security researchers handle sensitive data.
What if your AI could do it without sending
anything to the cloud?

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:14,010
This extension runs Gemini Nano 4 entirely on-device —
and only reaches for the cloud when it has to.

3
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:21,474
Load it in, hit Summarize.
The badge names the runtime that answered.

4
00:00:21,624 --> 00:00:28,938
On this machine the local model isn't loaded —
the engine routes the identical request to Gemini
in the cloud through Firebase AI Logic.

5
00:00:29,088 --> 00:00:36,402
Every click is live — nothing staged.
Same code paths a local model would take.

6
00:00:36,552 --> 00:00:47,382
Now the twist that makes this hybrid:
a full advisory, far beyond the local context window.

7
00:00:47,532 --> 00:00:58,362
The result is tagged CLOUD.
Same call, same interface —
on-device when feasible, cloud when needed.

8
00:00:58,512 --> 00:01:04,032
Four tools run through the same engine:

9
00:01:04,182 --> 00:01:09,702
Attack Scenario — the attack route in Google's reward format.

10
00:01:09,852 --> 00:01:15,371
Redact — scrubs emails, contact numbers, names.

11
00:01:15,521 --> 00:01:21,042
Severity — Critical to Info, with a one-line justification.

12
00:01:21,192 --> 00:01:29,194
One call into the Firebase AI Logic SDK.

13
00:01:29,344 --> 00:01:37,346
Two questions: is Nano available, does the text fit?

14
00:01:37,496 --> 00:01:45,498
Yes → local: confidential, free, offline.
No → the same call goes to Gemini in the cloud.

15
00:01:45,648 --> 00:01:52,490
Full source on GitHub — free software license.

16
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:59,482
Clone, install the libraries, load dist/ into Chrome.

17
00:01:59,632 --> 00:02:06,474
#BuildHybridAI 2026 — thanks for watching.

